-- title:
--   Commute GHalf Sandwich Error Bound
-- statement:
--   **The explicit half-sandwich envelope dominates the quadratic stage loss.**
--
--   Let $(m,q,d)$ have a field model, let $\gamma$ be any real error value, let $0\le\zeta\le1$, and let $k\in\mathbb N$. Define
--
--   $$
--   E_{\mathrm{pair}}=138m\left(\gamma^{1/16}+\zeta^{1/16}+(d/q)^{1/16}\right),
--   $$
--
--   and
--
--   $$
--   E_{\mathrm{half}}=426k^2m\left(\gamma^{1/16}+\zeta^{1/16}+(d/q)^{1/16}\right).
--   $$
--
--   Then
--
--   $$
--   3k\left(4k\zeta+kE_{\mathrm{pair}}\right)\le E_{\mathrm{half}}.
--   $$
--
--   This algebraic comparison absorbs the stagewise commutation and self-consistency losses into the error scale used by the full half-sandwich theorem.
--
--   Formalization credit: Sirui Lu, Ruixuan Deng, Yanqiao Zhu, and Zhengfeng Ji (arXiv:2609.19814). Mathematical source: Zhengfeng Ji, Anand Natarajan, Thomas Vidick, John Wright, and Henry Yuen (arXiv:2009.12982).
--
--   **Formalization Note.** The source declaration is `MIPStarRE.LDT.Pasting.commuteGHalfSandwich_error_bound`; its Lean statement gives the exact quantifier order and all boundary hypotheses.
